    <item>
      <title>The Folly of the Golden Deer</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the forest of Dvaitavana, the great warrior prince Arjuna encountered a magnificent golden deer. Its coat shone like the sun, its eyes sparkled with life. The deer seemed to embody the very essence of nature. Arjuna, ever the hunter, was drawn to the deer. But as he shot the arrow, he felt a pang of guilt. The deer&apos;s spirit, Rishyasringa, descended to the mortal realm, and Arjuna was overcome with remorse. He realized that his envy for the deer&apos;s beauty had led him to destroy it. The Rishi&apos;s words echoed in Arjuna&apos;s mind: &apos;Your envy has brought about your downfall.&apos; As the great warrior prince reflected on his actions, he understood that his pursuit of something external had blinded him to the beauty within himself. His envy had become his greatest enemy, and he vowed to never let it consume him again. This is Envy — the destructive force that turns us against ourselves. Today we covet status, possessions, and the validation of others — ask yourself, what is the true cost of your desires?</description>
